<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guido I da Polenta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1310">1310</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Guido da Polenta the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guido I da Polenta, called the Elder, was lord of Ravenna from 1275 to 1297 and founder of the da Polenta lordship. A Guelph leader, he took control of the city with the help of the Malatesta of Rimini, and sealed the alliance by marrying his daughter Francesca to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-malatesta">Giovanni Malatesta</a>. He later handed power to his sons and died in 1310.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guido-i-da-polenta.jpg" alt="Guido I da Polenta" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Mochi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Mochi_-_Dante_Alighieri_in_atto_di_presentare_Giotto_a_Guido_da_Polenta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
